WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.360
Celebrity detectives, suicidal&nbsp;
superheroes, and elementary school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.579
astronauts? Grab some popcorn and check&nbsp;
out the new gems Netflix has to offer.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.120
A hair-raising horror story, the&nbsp;
supernatural series "Archive 81"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.320
takes viewers on quite the thrill ride.&nbsp;
The show follows archivist Dan Turner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.680
played by Mamoudou Athie, who is tasked with&nbsp;
restoring tapes burned in an apartment fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.960
Working in an extremely desolate location,&nbsp;
Dan must also piece together any information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.840
he can about what actually happened during the&nbsp;
blaze. The more Dan uncovers from the footage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:41.200
which was filmed by Dina Shihabi's character,&nbsp;
Melody, the weirder circumstances get.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.720
Based on the 2016 podcast of the same name,&nbsp;
"Archive 81" has received high praise from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:52.570
critics and fans. Despite this success,&nbsp;
the series was canceled after one season.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.400
Spy thriller "In From the Cold" follows Jenny —&nbsp;
a.k.a. Anya — a Russian spy once known as "the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:04.480
Whisper" until she went into hiding in the United&nbsp;
States. Played by Margarita Levieva, Jenny is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:09.360
a divorced mother, who wants to prioritize her&nbsp;
family but gets pulled back into her old way of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.720
life when she's discovered and forced to embark&nbsp;
on a series of dangerous missions in Madrid.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:20.160
This spy thriller proves that a work-life balance&nbsp;
isn't always easy to achieve, especially when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:26.000
work portion revolves around guns, violence, and&nbsp;
being an all-out assassin. Though this might not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.880
be the most relatable sentiment, "In From the&nbsp;
Cold" is an enticing spy series that adds its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.250
own spin on the well-worn genre and hooks its&nbsp;
audience with a series of thrilling twists.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.560
If you're a an of oddball murder mysteries,&nbsp;
then "Murderville" is a must-watch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.520
This improvisation-driven comedy follows&nbsp;
mustache-twirling detective Terry Seattle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.360
played by "Arrested Development"&nbsp;
star Will Arnett, as he solves cases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.320
alongside celebrity guest stars and keeps&nbsp;
the audience laughing from start to finish.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.880
"Senior detective Terry Seattle.&nbsp;
And no, I've never been."

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.560
"Hm, that was gonna be my first question."

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.360
"'Course it was."

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:06.320
Without giving too much away, a few of Terry's&nbsp;
all-star assistants include Annie Murphy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:12.160
Ken Jeong, and Kumail Nanjiani. Since much of&nbsp;
the series is made up of unscripted elements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:17.350
these unsuspecting celebrities are taken on as&nbsp;
much of a comedy-filled ride as the audience.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.920
A crime mystery based in Indonesia,&nbsp;
"Photocopier" follows a young woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.480
named Sur, played by Shenina Cinnamon,&nbsp;
who encounters a worst-case scenario when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.720
a compromising selfie begins to make&nbsp;
its rounds after a night of drinking.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:36.080
The fallout is swift and severe as she loses&nbsp;
her scholarship and faces ridicule from her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.640
parents. Perhaps worst of all, she doesn't&nbsp;
remember the events of the night before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.840
Sur must retrace her steps to&nbsp;
figure out what really happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.880
a mystery that's flooded with blurred lines&nbsp;
and deception. "Photocopier" has seen screaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.200
success in reviews from critics and fans&nbsp;
alike, and it will have viewers on the edge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.467
of their seats while they try to piece together a&nbsp;
black-out-induced night with the main characters.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.560
If the title "The Woman in the House Across&nbsp;
the Street from the Girl in the Window" sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.680
familiar, it's because the series is a parody of&nbsp;
the Netflix thriller "The Woman in the Window"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.960
as well as other mystery psychological material&nbsp;
in the same vein. The film follows Anna,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.680
played by Kristen Bell, a grieving alcoholic&nbsp;
who believes she's witnessed a murder.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.840
Unfortunately, no one, including the&nbsp;
authorities, takes her seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:27.040
as she often has hallucinations. From a boring&nbsp;
existence staring out a window to solving a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.605
possible murder case on her own, Anna's life is&nbsp;
turned upside down in this dark comedy thriller.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:39.200
"I swear I know what I saw,&nbsp;
okay? I saw her dying."

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.680
Though spoofs tend to be flooded with clichés,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.958
this latest parody installment is worth a&nbsp;
watch for comedy and thriller fans alike.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.080
"Windfall" follows a man,&nbsp;
known simply as the robber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.520
who breaks into a vacation home&nbsp;
owned by a well-to-do couple.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.600
When the husband and wife arrive at their&nbsp;
getaway home, instead of fleeing the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.960
the robber decides to take the two hostage inside&nbsp;
their own house. The heist slowly falls apart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:07.920
as it's revealed that this particular married&nbsp;
couple aren't exactly living in marital bliss.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.240
Despite the film's simplistic nature,&nbsp;
"Windfall" is gifted with an explosive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:17.200
cast, featuring Jason Segel as the&nbsp;
robber, Lily Collins as the wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:22.560
and Jesse Plemons as the CEO. As John&nbsp;
Nugent of Empire Magazine observes,

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.040
"Short, sharp and mostly satisfying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.342
this is a thriller that sticks to the&nbsp;
stripped-back fundamentals of the genre."

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:34.880
Imagine being 10 years old and getting recruited&nbsp;
by NASA to go on a secret mission to the moon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.160
That's exactly what happens to&nbsp;
protagonist Stan in "Apollo 10½:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.520
A Space Age Childhood," which intertwines&nbsp;
a nostalgic depiction of growing up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.560
1960s Houston with a fanciful story&nbsp;
about becoming a child astronaut.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:53.760
Boasting a gifted cast featuring Glen&nbsp;
Powell, Jack Black, and Zachary Levi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:58.640
it's no wonder why this film received high&nbsp;
praise from audience members and critics alike.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:03.600
Though "Apollo 10½: A Space Age Childhood"&nbsp;
might be most appealing to baby boomers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.440
its riveting animation and creative&nbsp;
storytelling make it enjoyable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.280
viewing for all ages.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.440
With a resume including unauthorized spoofs&nbsp;
of "The Punisher" and "Power Rangers,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:18.480
as well as well-received adaptations of "Dredd"&nbsp;
and "Castlevania," Adi Shankar has breathed new,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:23.840
revisionist life into familiar genre fare. His&nbsp;
latest work, the partially animated series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.640
"The Guardians of Justice (Will Save You),"&nbsp;
specifically celebrates superhero series like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.120
DC Comics and Warner Brothers' deadly&nbsp;
serious "Justice League'' franchise.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.280
The story begins in the late 1980s,&nbsp;
following a long period of global&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:42.000
peace when extraterrestrial superhero&nbsp;
Marvelous Man, played by Will Yun Lee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:47.200
saved the planet from the clutches of Robo-Hitler&nbsp;
and a deadly Third World War. When Marvelous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:52.160
Man dies of an apparent suicide, his former&nbsp;
teammate Knight Hawk begins investigating his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:56.560
late captain's passing. Should Knight Hawk&nbsp;
and the other Guardians fail to rise to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:02.773
challenge and fill the void left by Marvelous Man,&nbsp;
Earth could face yet another global catastrophe.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:08.560
Following his long run as a creator, producer,&nbsp;
and showrunner on HBO's epic fantasy series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:13.520
"Game of Thrones" D.B. Weiss went the completely&nbsp;
opposite direction with his next project:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:19.040
a charming, musically oriented high school comedy&nbsp;
called "Metal Lords." In this Netflix film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:24.560
Hunter, played by Adrian Greensmith, is a&nbsp;
devotee of the darkest and hardest heavy metal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:28.160
and he desperately wants to start&nbsp;
a band. In pursuit of his dream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.800
he recruits his best friend and marching&nbsp;
band percussionist, Kevin, to play drums.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.200
"Meet me after school. We've got work to do."

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:38.400
"Metal Lords" tracks the duo's&nbsp;
progress as they find their sound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.080
transform an overstressed orchestra&nbsp;
cellist into a metal bassist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:46.800
and prepare for an impending Battle of the&nbsp;
Bands. Wholesome and nostalgic, "Metal Lords"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:52.650
feels simultaneously familiar and unique in its&nbsp;
portrayal of high school friendships and romances.

